menu "Deco Optimizer"

    config DECO_HEADLESS
        bool "Headless build (no display, touch or LVGL)"
        default n
        help
            Builds without the screen, touch input and LVGL, replacing them with no-op stubs. Status and control are then
            on the web page, over MQTT/Home Assistant and in the serial log only. This frees roughly 50 KB of RAM.
            Requires DECO_SETUP_AP_PASSWORD, because a headless device has no screen to show a setup password on.

    config DECO_SETUP_AP_PASSWORD
        string "Setup access point password (8-63 characters)"
        default ""
        help
            Password for the first-run setup Wi-Fi network (Deco-Setup-XXXX). It only guards the setup window, which
            is open until the Wi-Fi details are entered, so choose something other than the default you may have seen
            elsewhere. Required for headless builds. On builds with a screen, leave it empty to use a random
            password shown on the display (as a QR code and as text).

    config DECO_RESET_BUTTON_GPIO
        int "GPIO of the setup-reset button (-1 to disable)"
        range -1 48
        default 9 if IDF_TARGET_ESP32C3 || IDF_TARGET_ESP32C6
        default 0
        help
            Holding this pin low for 5 seconds while the firmware is running clears the Wi-Fi details and restarts into
            setup mode. This is normally the board's BOOT button. Holding it during reset instead enters the ROM
            download mode, so it only acts once the firmware is running. Set -1 on boards without a button.

    config DECO_SCREENSAVER_TIMEOUT_S
        int "Screensaver timeout in seconds (0 disables)"
        range 0 86400
        default 300
        depends on !DECO_HEADLESS
        help
            After this long without a touch the screen shows a short burst of "snow" and the backlight turns off.
            A touch wakes it (the wake touch is not passed to the interface), and so does every scan or optimise run.
            Not used during first-run setup, so the QR code stays on screen. Headless builds have no screen.

endmenu
